<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Niagara River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Niagara River flows about 58 km north from Lake Erie to Lake <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ontario">Ontario</a>, forming part of the border between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-midway">Midway</a> along its course it drops over Niagara Falls. Its banks were home to the Neutral Confederacy before about 1650 and later became a frontier contested in the colonial wars and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-1812">War of 1812</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/niagara-river.jpg" alt="Niagara River" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Reading Tom from Reading, UK · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Whirlpool_Bridge_(2936545446).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
